sses `skillLabel: skillLabelFor(result)`, add `degraded: result.metrics.degraded === true`. Leave the other calls, which report a skip or an outage with no answer. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `V tests/hooks/claude-user-prompt-submit-hook.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c \"degraded: result.metrics.degraded === true\" $UPS` prints 1.\n104: - [x] T020 [P] Report the degraded share and the newest record time in `advisor_status` (`ST`, `SCH`, `STT`). In `SCH`, add `rollingDegradedRate: z.number().min(0).max(1)` and `lastRecordAt: z.string()` to the `hookHealth` object and keep `.strict()`. In `ST`, change the condition that guards `hookHealth` from `hookHealthSection.lastInvocations.length > 0` to `hookHealthSection.lastRecordAt !== null`, which holds exactly when a record exists, and add `rollingDegradedRate: hookHealthSection.rollingDegradedRate` and `lastRecordAt: hookHealthSection.lastRecordAt` to the block. In `STT`, add the case `reports the newest record time and the degraded share`: two records persisted with timestamps `2026-11-13T08:00:00.000Z` (carrying `degraded: true`) and `2026-11-13T08:00:05.000Z`, then `readAdvisorStatus` gives `hookHealth.lastRecordAt` `2026-11-13T08:00:05.000Z` and `rollingDegradedRate` 0.5, and `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse` accepts the output. Verify: `V tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n105: - [x] T021 [P] Let the top hub name its routed command when only a lower row carries it (`REC`, `RCT`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, change the guard `command && !alreadyOffered.has(command)` to `command && (!alreadyOffered.has(command) || (topOnly && index === 0))`. Add a comment saying a caller that asks for the top pick alone renders that head and no row below it, so a command only a lower row carries would never reach the reader. In `RCT`, add a case after `never offers one command through both its own row and the owning hub`: read the `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` row from `scripts/routing-accur